<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pomorie</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anchialos, Anchialus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anchialus, now Pomorie, is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, founded in antiquity as a Greek colony of Apollonia. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a Byzantine fortress on the frontier with Bulgaria and changed hands repeatedly. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> won a battle near it in 763, and Simeon I destroyed a Byzantine army by the nearby river Achelous in 917.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pomorie.jpg" alt="Pomorie" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boby Dimitrov from Sofia, Bulgaria · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Town_of_Pomorie_aerial_Boby_Dimitrov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
